          "text": [
            {
              "text": "2.1.2.2. Conduct knowledge training with the trainee using the AFQTP. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-62",
          "pageNumber": 4,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "2.1.2.3. Answer questions for the trainee to ensure the required task knowledge has been  gained to complete the task. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-63",
          "pageNumber": 4,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "2.1.2.4. Sign-off the task(s). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-64",
          "pageNumber": 4,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "2.1.3. The Certifier shall: ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-65",
          "pageNumber": 4,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "2.1.3.1. Evaluate the Airman’s task performance without assistance. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-66",
          "pageNumber": 4,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "2.1.3.2. Sign-off the task(s). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "h-3",
          "level": 1,
          "pageNumber": 4,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "Section 3—INTRODUCTION ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "heading",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-67",
          "pageNumber": 4,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.1. Objectives. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-68",
          "pageNumber": 4,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.1.1. In accordance with (IAW) Department of Defense Instruction (DoDI) 6055.04, DoD  Motor Vehicle and Traffic Safety, the DoD Components will provide training to operators of  government-owned full-size vans, stressing the unique handling characteristics of these  vehicles.  In addition, large Sport Utility Vehicles (SUV) and like vehicles operated by the  DAF pose unique handling characteristics and is subject to this training.  This training will be  at the government’s expense. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-69",
          "pageNumber": 4,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.1.2. Given lectures, demonstrations, hands-on driving session and a performance test,  trainees will be able to perform operator’s inspection and complete the performance test with  zero instructor assists. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-70",
          "pageNumber": 4,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.1.2.1. Train and qualify each trainee in safe operation and preventive maintenance of  various full-size vans. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-71",
          "pageNumber": 4,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.1.2.2. This training will ensure the trainee becomes a qualified full-size van operator; an  operator who has the knowledge and skills to operate a full-size van in a safe and  professional manner. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-72",
          "pageNumber": 4,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.2. Desired Learning Outcomes. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 4,
