    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p-137",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.2.3.7. Curb Weight:  4,965 lbs. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-138",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.2.3.8. Gross Vehicle Weight Rating (GVWR):  9,600 lbs. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-139",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.2.3.9. Gross Axle Weight Rating (GAWR) Front:  4,600 lbs. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-140",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.2.3.10.   GAWR Rear:  6,084 lbs. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-141",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.2.4. The 4WD System.  A vehicle equipped with 4WD has the ability to use all four wheels  to power itself.  This increases traction which may enable the vehicle to safely drive over  terrain and road conditions that a conventional two-wheel drive vehicle cannot. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-142",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "Figure 5.1.  The 4WD System. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "altText": undefined,
          "caption": undefined,
          "id": "fig-4",
          "imageId": "p8-xobj-Im0",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "type": "figure",
          "unsupported": false,
        },
        {
          "id": "p-143",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.2.4.1. Power is supplied to all four wheels through a transfer case or power transfer unit.   4WD vehicles allow the operator to select different drive modes as necessary. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-144",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.2.4.2. Refer to the manufacturer’s operator’s manual for information on shifting  procedures and maintenance. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-145",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.2.4.3. On some 4WD models, the initial shift from two-wheel drive to 4WD while the  vehicle is moving can cause a momentary clunk and ratcheting sound.  These sounds are  normal as the front drivetrain comes up to speed and is not cause for concern. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-146",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.3. Vehicle Inspection. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-147",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.3.1. Types of Vehicle Inspection.  Note:  If discrepancies are found they must be reported  to the Vehicle Control Official (VCO), the supervisor, and/or vehicle maintenance. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-148",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.3.1.1. Pre-trip inspection – find items/problems that could cause accident or breakdown. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-149",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.3.1.1.1.   Vehicle maintenance to authorize continued use for all other maintenance  discrepancies. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-150",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.3.1.1.2.   Cleanliness/damage/missing items. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-151",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.3.1.1.3.   Leaks (fuel/oil/coolant/hydraulic/air). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-152",
          "pageNumber": 8,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.3.1.1.4.   Fluid Levels; ensure level is within limits: ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
      ],
