    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p-216",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.1.5. Operator and passengers shall wear seat belts as provided. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-217",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.1.6. No passengers shall be allowed to ride anywhere, except in the main cab of the  full-size van. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-218",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.1.7. Minimize or eliminate the need for backing.  Always check to the rear before  backing, and use a spotter if needed/available. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-219",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.1.8. Be aware of personnel in the work zone. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-220",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.1.9. Full-size van speed should be adjusted for load, traffic and weather. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-221",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.1.10.   Do not leave the full-size van unattended with the engine running.  Shut-off the  engine and set the parking brake when the full-size van is not in use. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-222",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.1.11.   Never refuel in a closed building. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-223",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.1.12.   Do not allow riders aboard while being towed. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-224",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.1.13.   Yield the right of way to ambulances, fire trucks, or other vehicles in emergency  situations. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-225",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2. Tire changing safety. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-226",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.1. Consider where the vehicle is located.  If on a bridge, curve, road with no  shoulder, etc.; it is safer to move a vehicle on a flat tire to a safe location. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-227",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.2. Find a location with a firm and level surface for the jack. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-228",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.3. Turn-on the four-way flashers. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-229",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.4. Place warning triangles or flares. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-230",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.5. Block the wheels.  If changing a front tire, block the rear wheels.  If changing a  rear tire, block the front wheels. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-231",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.6. Place the vehicle in “Park” if it has an automatic transmission and low gear if it  has a standard shift.  Set parking brake. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-232",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.7. Ensure the jack is rated for the weight of the vehicle. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-233",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.8. Ensure proper placement of jack. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-234",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.9. If available, use jack stands after lifting the vehicle. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-235",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.10.   Once the vehicle is lifted; never at any time get under the vehicle. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 12,
