    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p-236",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.11.   Before removing lug nuts, ensure lug wedges are loose (double check). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-237",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.12.   After changing the tire, return the jack and lug wrench to the location  recommended by the manufacturer (keep them from becoming flying projectiles and makes  them available for future tire changes). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-238",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.2.13.   Secure the damaged tire and once it is repaired, return the spare tire back to its  proper location. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-239",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.3. Foreign Object Damage (FOD). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-240",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.3.1. Vehicle operators will remove FOD from tires during daily the vehicle inspection.   Before entering the airfield, a physical check for loose/unsecured objects and an inspection  of the tire treads for FOD will be accomplished, with the exception of emergency vehicles  responding to actual situations. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-241",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.3.2. Any vehicle which has been driven on an unpaved surface will have a tire FOD  inspection accomplished prior to re-entering the airfield area.  Vehicles that frequent the  flight line will be equipped with a FOD picker and a covered FOD container. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-242",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.3.3. FOD picker will be etched with the vehicle number painted on. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-243",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.3.4. FOD containers will be identified with the letters "FOD" and will be emptied  daily. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-244",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.5.3.5. FOD checks are performed so that aircraft damage can be kept at a minimum. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-245",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.6. High Rollover Risk. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-246",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.6.1. Rollover facts: ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-247",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.6.1.1. According to the United States Department of Transportation (DoT), traffic  crashes are preventable but continue to be a leading cause of death in the United States,  claiming approximately 37,000 lives annually. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-248",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.6.1.2. Some 60,501 traffic crash fatalities occurred in 2022, with occupants of passenger  vehicles (passenger cars and light trucks) accounting for 45,856, about 76 percent of the  total.  Rollover crashes are a significant and growing contributor to this statistic.  A rollover  crash is particularly violent in nature. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-249",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "5.6.1.3. Unrestrained occupants of a vehicle that rolls are subjected to a variety of forces  and impacts that can result in severe injuries or death.  In 2022, rollover crashes killed  nearly 9,000 occupants, two-fifths of the total deaths of occupants of these types of  vehicles. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 13,
      "warnings": [
