              ],
            },
          ],
          "type": "table",
        },
        {
          "id": "h-14",
          "level": 2,
          "pageNumber": 9,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.4. Fall Protection Program. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "heading",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-226",
          "pageNumber": 9,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.4.1. Unit Fall Protection Policy. A policy statement will be developed that states the Commander’s  commitment to providing a safe workplace for employees working at heights. The policy will also  provide general goals and guidance for the fall protection program. An example statement can be found  in ANSI/ASSP Z359.2-2023, Minimum Requirements for a Comprehensive Managed Fall Protection  Program (DAFMAN 91-203, 13.3.1.). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-227",
          "pageNumber": 9,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.4.2. Unit Fall Protection Program Administration. The unit fall protection program will be  administered and managed by a Competent Person. (DAFMAN 91-203, 13.3.2.2.). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 9,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "h-15",
          "level": 2,
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5. Roles and Responsibilities. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "heading",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-228",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.1. Unit Commander. The unit commander is ultimately responsible for the development and  implementation of the fall protection program that promotes a safe and healthful workplace (DAFMAN  91-203, 13.3.2.1.).  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-229",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.1.1. The competent person will be identified in writing by the unit commander and meet the  requirements of ANSI/ASSP Z359.0 and ANSI/ASSP Z359.2 (DAFMAN 91-203, 13.3.2.2.). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-230",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.2. Installation Occupational Safety. The Installation Occupational Safety office will provide advice  and guidance to the Unit Fall Protection Program Administrator. (DAFMAN 91-203, 13.3.2.6.). These  duties include: ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-231",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.2.1. Assisting in fall hazard surveys and development of written fall protection and rescue  procedures to ensure rescue procedures, equipment, and training meet fall protection requirements. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-232",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.2.2. Identifying unabated fall hazards and providing/tracking a Risk Assessment Codes (RACs). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-233",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.2.3. Conduct thorough annual review of fall protection program elements and documents  annually in safety inspection/assessment reports.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-234",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.3. Fire & Emergency Services (F&ES) Flight. The F&ES Flight will assist in the fall hazard surveys  and development of written fall protection and rescue procedures (DAFMAN 91-203, 13.3.2.7).  Additionally, the F&ES Flight: ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-235",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.3.1. Will ensure equipment and training meet fall protection requirements.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-236",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.3.2. May also act as the competent rescuer when they meet the requirements as defined in  ANSI/ASSP Z359.0 to perform rescue at height when included in the organizational rescue plan  and agreed to by the installation fire chief. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-237",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.4. Authorized Rescuers. Authorized rescuers will meet the definition outlined in ANSI/ASSP  Z359.0 and meet all applicable responsibilities in ANSI/ASSP Z359.2 (DAFMAN 91-203, 13.3.2.8). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-238",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.5. Supervisors. IAW DAFMAN 91-203, 13.3.2.9., supervisors shall: ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-239",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.5.1. Ensure each authorized, qualified, and competent person using a fall protection/fall arrest  system is trained and evaluated on proper use, application, and inspection of fall protection/fall  arrest systems.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-240",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.5.2. Be familiar with the shop’s typical work assignments and fall protection/fall arrest systems  required. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-241",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.5.3. Be responsible for the procurement of fall protection/fall arrest systems required by the  organization or shop as directed by the qualified person. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-242",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.5.4. Be able to provide recommendations for qualified and competent personnel in the  organization to the unit commander. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-243",
          "pageNumber": 10,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.5.5. Be designated in writing by the unit commander. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 10,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p-244",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.5.6. A supervisor may also be a qualified, competent and/or authorized person if they meet the  training requirements listed in DAFMAN 91-203, 13.7. Training.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-245",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.6. Trainers. Trainers will be designated in writing by the unit commander (DAFMAN 91-203,  13.3.2.10). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-246",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.7. Qualified Person. A qualified person supports the fall protection program with expertise in  various areas such as engineering and system design. IAW DAFMAN 91-203, 13.3.2.3., ANSI/ASSP  Z359.0, and ANSI Z359.2-2017 the qualified person shall: ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-247",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.7.1. Be designated in writing by the unit commander.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-248",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.7.2. Be trained and meet the responsibilities outlined in ANSI/ASSP Z359.2 and as defined in  29 CFR 1910.21(b), Definitions.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-249",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.7.3. Supervise the design, selection, installation, use, and inspection of anchorages and  horizontal lifelines. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-250",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.7.4. Calculates, tests, and publishes proper procedures for utilizing PFAS equipment. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-251",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.7.5. Certify anchorages below 5000lbs.; HOWEVER, must be rated for a safety factor of 2. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-252",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.7.6. Participate in the investigation of all incidents related to falls from heights as required. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-253",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8. Competent Person. A competent person supervises, implements, and monitors the fall protection  program. Usually a supervisor or manager, they have more experience in fall protection than authorized  persons and can halt work if safety concerns arise. IAW DAFMAN 91-203, 13.3.2.4., ANSI/ASSP  Z359.0, and ANSI Z359.2-2017, the competent person shall: ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-254",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.1. Be designated in writing by the unit commander. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-255",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.2. Be trained and meet the responsibilities outlined in ANSI/ASSP Z359.2 and as defined in  29 CFR 1910.140(b), Definitions. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-256",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.3. Supervise, implement, and monitor the fall protection program. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-257",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.4. Periodically inspect all fall protection equipment. To include anchors, body harness, and  connectors of the fall protection program. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-258",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.5. Conduct initial Fall Hazard Survey (See Chapter 4). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-259",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.6. Identify, evaluate, and impose limits, controls, and monitor swing falls. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-260",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.7. Has authority to STOP work immediately and take prompt corrective actions. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-261",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.8. Implement a fall protection plan and rescue plan. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-262",
          "pageNumber": 11,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.9. Participates in the investigation of all mishaps related to falls from heights. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 11,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p-263",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.10. Verifies PFAS have been installed and inspected per manufacturer’s instructions.  Immediately remove from service all damaged PFAS components or components subjected to the  forces of arresting a fallen person. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-264",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.11. Verifies training of authorized persons on fall protection and rescue procedures ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-265",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.12. Establishes clearance requirements prior to authorized persons starting work. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-266",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.8.13. Supervise the selection, installation, use, and inspection of anchorages (≥5000 lbs.) in  consultation with the program administrator and qualified person. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-267",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.9. Authorized Person. An authorized person understands their employer’s policies and procedures  regarding fall protection and follows instructions from the competent person. IAW DAFMAN 91-203,  13.3.2.5., 29 CFR 1910.21(b), ANSI/ASSP Z359.0, ANSI/ASSP Z359.2, and ANSI Z359.2-2017, the  competent person shall: ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-268",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.9.1. Alert the competent person about any unsafe conditions before starting work. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-269",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.9.2. Properly use, inspect, maintain, store, and care for fall protection equipment. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-270",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.5.9.3. Inspect all fall protection equipment prior to use and notify the competent person of any  defects or damage. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "h-16",
          "level": 2,
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6 Training Requirements. Before employees are exposed to a fall hazard, training shall be  completed IAW 29 CFR 1910.30, Training Requirements (DAFMAN 91-203, 13.7). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "heading",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-271",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.1. Trainers conducting fall protection and rescue training shall meet the requirements of  ANSI/ASSP Z490.1.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-272",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.2. Authorized personnel will be trained by a Competent or Qualified person trainer IAW  ANSI/ASSP Z359.2. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-273",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.3. Program administrators shall be trained on all equipment and practices applicable to the scope of  work IAW ANSI/ASSP Z359.2. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-274",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.4. Retraining. IAW 29 CFR 1910.30(c), the employer must retrain an employee when the employer  has reason to believe the employee does not have the understanding and skill required by 29 CFR  1910.30(a) and 1910.30(b). Situations requiring retraining include, but are not limited to, the following: ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-275",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.4.1. When changes in the workplace render previous training obsolete or inadequate. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-276",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.4.2. When changes in the types of fall protection systems or equipment to be used render  previous training obsolete or inadequate. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-277",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.4.3. When inadequacies in an affected employee's knowledge or use of fall protection systems  or equipment indicate that the employee no longer has the requisite understanding or skill necessary  to use equipment or perform the job safely. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-278",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.5. Recurring Training.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-279",
          "pageNumber": 12,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.5.1. Recurring training shall be performed at least annually.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 12,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p-280",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.5.2. The training shall establish employee proficiency, include an in-depth review of current  and previous procedures, and introduce a new or revised control methods and procedures, as  necessary. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-281",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.5.3. Personnel trained as Competent and Authorized persons shall be retrained at least every  two years. Annual refresher training shall be conducted the year following attendance in the initial  course. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-282",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.5.4. Competent and Authorized persons who are also identified as rescuers must meet all  Authorized Rescuers training requirements as identified in DAFMAN 91-203, 13.3.2.8. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-283",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.6.6. Training Documentation. All training shall be documented in accordance with DAFI 91-202,  with the required information detailed in OSHA Publication 2254, Training Requirements in OSHA  Standards.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "h-17",
          "level": 2,
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.7. Fall Protection Plans. Fall protection plans will be used only in construction, for residential roofs,  leading edge work and precast concrete erection work (DAFMAN 91-203, 13.6). ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "heading",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-284",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.7.1. The written plan shall be coordinated with the installation Occupational Safety Office (or  applicable tenant Safety office) before the plan and its procedural controls are used.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-285",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.7.2. When it is determined to not be feasible to use fall protection systems while on residential roofs  as identified in 29 CFR 1910.28(b)(1)(ii), a written fall protection plan, meeting the requirements of 29  CFR 1926.502(k) and coordinated with the installation Occupational Safety Office, shall be developed.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-286",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.7.3. Training for the fall protection plan must meet the requirements of 29 CFR 1926.503(a) and  1926.503(c).  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-287",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.7.4. A corrective action plan will be accomplished describing planned upgrades (equipment, cost, and  timetable, prioritized by the shop) and appropriate RAC, to eliminate need partially or totally for  procedural controls.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-288",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.7.5. Consistent with OSHA guidelines, cost shall not be a consideration for selecting the fall  protection plan’s procedural controls versus implementing fall protection. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "h-18",
          "level": 2,
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.8. Fall Mishap Reporting.  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "heading",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-289",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.8.1. Falls from heights, regardless of whether an injury or damage has occurred, will be reported to  the servicing Occupational Safety Office, and investigated by a competent person, and occupational  safety personnel. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-290",
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.8.2. A mishap investigation will be accomplished to determine the cause of the fall and used to correct  any issues found in procedures, equipment, or rescue, as applicable. ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "h-19",
          "level": 2,
          "pageNumber": 13,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "3.9. Visual Aids. These visual aids provide supplementary resources, including OSHA letters of  interpretation, technical manual sections, and explanations of fall protection training requirements for both  general industry and construction settings, as well as clarification on the definition of a "qualified trainer." ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "heading",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 13,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p-291",
          "pageNumber": 14,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "Visual Aid. ",
            },
            {
