    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "h-147",
          "level": 1,
          "pageNumber": 65,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "Attachment 2  ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "heading",
        },
        {
          "id": "p-907",
          "pageNumber": 65,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "KNOWLEDGE CHECK ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-1",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-908",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "1. What is the primary purpose of fall protection equipment? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-1",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-909",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To enhance worker productivity. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-2",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-910",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To mitigate the effect of falls. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-3",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-911",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To protect employees from serious injury or death that need to work in elevated locations which  meet the OSHA trigger heights. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-4",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 65,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-2",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-912",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "2. IAW DAFMAN 91-203, what is the role of a Competent Person in the unit fall protection program? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-5",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-913",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Conducting fall hazard surveys. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-6",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-914",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Providing advice to the unit commander ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-7",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-915",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Administer and Manage the Unit Fall Protection Program.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-8",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 65,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-3",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-916",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "3. IAW DAFMAN 91-203, who is ultimately responsible for the development and implementation of  the fall protection program that promotes a safe and healthful workplace? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-9",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-917",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Qualified Person ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-10",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-918",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Competent Person ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-11",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-919",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Unit Commander ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-12",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 65,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-4",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-920",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "4. True or False: Duties of the Installation Occupational Safety office include conducting thorough  annual review of fall protection program elements. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-13",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-921",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. True ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-14",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-922",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. False  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-15",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 65,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-5",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-923",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "5. Who assists in the fall hazard surveys and development of written fall protection and rescue  procedures? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-16",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-924",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Fire & Emergency Services (F&ES) Flight ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-17",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-925",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Unit Commander ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-18",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-926",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Authorized Rescuer ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-19",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 65,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-6",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-927",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "6. IAW DAFMAN 91-203, supervisor responsibilities include? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-20",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-928",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Responsible for the procurement of fall protection/fall arrest systems. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-21",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-929",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Designation in writing by the Competent Person. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-22",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-930",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Delegates rescue team personnel. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-23",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 65,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-7",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-931",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "7. What is a common requirement for Trainers, Qualified, and Competent persons? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-24",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-932",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Designated in writing by the unit commander. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-25",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-933",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Participate in the investigation of all incidents related to falls. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-26",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-934",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Implement a fall protection plan and rescue plan. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-27",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 65,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-8",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-935",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "8. When is fall protection retraining required? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-28",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-936",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. When changes in the workplace render previous training obsolete or inadequate. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-29",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-937",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Only if there is an injury. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-30",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-938",
                  "pageNumber": 65,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Once every three years. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-31",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 65,
          "type": "list",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 65,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "list-9",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-939",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "9. How often should recurring training be performed? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-32",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-940",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Quarterly ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-33",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-941",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Every 2 years ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-34",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-942",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Annually ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-35",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 66,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-10",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-943",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "10. With what agency shall the Fall Protection Plan be coordinated? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-36",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-944",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Commander ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-37",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-945",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Occupational Safety Office ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-38",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-946",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. F&ES Flight ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-39",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 66,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-11",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-947",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "11. In what situations should falls from heights be reported? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-40",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-948",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Only if there is an injury. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-41",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-949",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Regardless of whether an injury or damage has occurred. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-42",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-950",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Only if damage to property occurs. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-43",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 66,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-12",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-951",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "12. What is the purpose of a Fall Hazard Survey? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-44",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-952",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To determine the basic configuration of fall hazards. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-45",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-953",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To identify environmental factors affecting fall protection systems. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-46",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-954",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To help employers and safety professionals identify potential fall hazards and determine the  necessary steps to mitigate or eliminate them.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-47",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 66,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-13",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-955",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "13. IAW DAFMAN 91-203 who typically leads the fall hazard survey team? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-48",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-956",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Competent or Qualified Person(s) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-49",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-957",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Work Center Supervisors ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-50",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-958",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Installation Occupational Safety Office ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-51",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 66,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-14",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-959",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "14. True or False: A key aspects of a comprehensive Fall Hazard Survey is environmental factors  affecting the installation, use, inspection, maintenance, and dismantling of any fall protection system. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-52",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-960",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. True  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-53",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-961",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. False  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-54",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 66,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-15",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-962",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "15. The Fall Protection Program Assessment final report will be routed to the unit commander for review  and signature within how many days of completion? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-55",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-963",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. 5 ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-56",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-964",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. 10  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-57",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-965",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. 30 ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-58",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 66,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-16",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-966",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "16. IAW DAFI 91-202 how often will the installation or tenant unit’s Occupational Safety Office  complete an assessment of Fall Protection Program requirements for each unit? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-59",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-967",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Annually  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-60",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-968",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Quarterly ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-61",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-969",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Every 2 years ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-62",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 66,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-17",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-970",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "17. IAW DAFMAN 91-203 a Rescue Plan will include all the following EXCEPT? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-63",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-971",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Procedures to contact the rescue agency if a fall occurs. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-64",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-972",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Actions to be taken by the organization to rescue fallen authorized personnel, when possible. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-65",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-973",
                  "pageNumber": 66,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Steps to take when work is completed, e.g., clean up, storage.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-66",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 66,
          "type": "list",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 66,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "list-18",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-974",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "18. What are the SIGNS of suspension trauma? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-67",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-975",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Increased heart rate and high blood pressure. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-68",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-976",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Severe headache and muscle pain. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-69",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-977",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Faintness, nausea, breathlessness, and dizziness.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-70",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 67,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-19",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-978",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "19. What are some examples of a fallen worker secondary hazards? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-71",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-979",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Broken bones, entanglement, shock.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-72",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-980",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Heartburn, nausea, indigestion. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-73",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-981",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Sore throat, runny nose, cough.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-74",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 67,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-20",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-982",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "20. What is the primary approach outlined in the Hierarchy of Fall Protection for addressing fall hazards? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-75",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-983",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Fall Arrest Systems ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-76",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-984",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Administrative Controls ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-77",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-985",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Hazard Elimination  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-78",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 67,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-21",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-986",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "21. According to the Hierarchy of Fall Protection, which control method involves creating physical  barriers to prevent falls? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-79",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-987",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Fall Restraint Systems ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-80",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-988",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Passive Fall Protection  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-81",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-989",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Administrative Controls ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-82",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 67,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-22",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-990",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "22. Which type of fall protection involves devices like guardrails and nets that prevent falls but are not  directly connected to the employee? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-83",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-991",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Suspension System. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-84",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-992",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Passive Fall Protection.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-85",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-993",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Positioning System. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-86",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 67,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-23",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-994",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "23. What is the purpose of a Retrieval System in fall protection? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-87",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-995",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To restrict an employee's range of movement. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-88",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-996",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To provide prompt rescue of employees in the event of a fall.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-89",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-997",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To allow employees to lift and lower themselves along a vertical surface. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-90",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 67,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-24",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-998",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "24. True or False: There are NO exceptions to fall protection? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-91",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-999",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "D. True ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-92",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1000",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "E. False  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-93",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 67,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-25",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1001",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "25. Which of the following materials is NOT suitable for connectors in personal fall protection systems? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-94",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1002",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Stainless Steel ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-95",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1003",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Natural fiber  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-96",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1004",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Steel ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-97",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 67,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-26",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1005",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "26. What system consists of a body harness, anchorage, and connector? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-98",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1006",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. PFAS  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-99",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1007",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Positioning Systems ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-100",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1008",
                  "pageNumber": 67,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Rope Descent System ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-101",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 67,
          "type": "list",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 67,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "list-27",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1009",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "27. IAW 29 CFR 1910.21 which of the following is NOT part of a Rope Descent System? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-102",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1010",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Descent device ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-103",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1011",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Horizontal lifeline  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-104",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1012",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Chair (seatboard). ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-105",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 68,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-28",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1013",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "28. What is the purpose of a travel restraint system? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-106",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1014",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To arrest an employee in a fall. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-107",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1015",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To eliminate the possibility of an employee going over the edge of a walking-working surface.  (pg. 30) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-108",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1016",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To provide support on an elevated vertical surface. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-109",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 68,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-29",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1017",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "29. Which lifeline system is primarily used for tasks that require workers to move horizontally over a  large area without constantly disconnecting and reattaching to different anchor points? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-110",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1018",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Portable Gantry ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-111",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1019",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Horizontal Lifeline  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-112",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1020",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Rigid Rail System ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-113",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 68,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-30",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1021",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "30. Which lifeline system is typically used in environments like warehouses and factories, providing fall  arrest solutions with short arrest distances? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-114",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1022",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Horizontal Lifeline ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-115",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1023",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Rigid Rail System  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-116",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1024",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Portable Gantry ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-117",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 68,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-31",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1025",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "31. IAW 29 CFR 1910.21, what defines a low-slope roof? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-118",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1026",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Any roof with a slope greater than 4-foot in 12-foot. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-119",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1027",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Any roof that is flat or less than or equal to a ratio of 4-foot in 12-foot.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-120",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1028",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Any roof with a slope greater than 6-foot in 12-foot. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-121",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 68,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-32",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1029",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "32. In webbing material, which material is more durable and rigid than nylon, and resists water  absorption? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-122",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1030",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Polyester  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-123",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1031",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Nylon ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-124",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1032",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Chemical resistant ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-125",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 68,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-33",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1033",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "33. When inspecting a lanyard prior to use, where should the inspection begin? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-126",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1034",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. In the middle of the lanyard. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-127",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1035",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. At one end of the lanyard working towards the other end.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-128",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1036",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. From the hardware towards the rope or strap. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-129",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 68,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-34",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1037",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "34. What is the primary purpose of the impact indicator on a self-retracting device? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-130",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1038",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To determine the device's maximum allowable weight. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-131",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1039",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To signal whether the device has been exposed to fall forces and should be retired.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-132",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1040",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To identify the manufacturer of the device. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-133",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 68,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-35",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1041",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "35. IAW 29 CFR 1910.140, anchorages used to attach personal fall protection equipment must be capable  of supporting at least how many pounds for each attached employee? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-134",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1042",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. 5,000 pounds.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-135",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1043",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. 7,500 pounds. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-136",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1044",
                  "pageNumber": 68,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. 10,000 pounds. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-137",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 68,
          "type": "list",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 68,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "list-36",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1045",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "36. IAW 29 CFR 1910.140, connectors must have a finish that is? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-138",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1046",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Painted. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-139",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1047",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Galvanized. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-140",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1048",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Corrosion-resistant.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-141",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 69,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-37",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1049",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "37. True or False: Maximum Arresting Force (MAF) refers to the highest force exerted on the body when  stopping a fall? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-142",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1050",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. True  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-143",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1051",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. False ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-144",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 69,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-38",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1052",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "38. What is the primary purpose of calculating fall clearance in a fall protection system? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-145",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1053",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To assess the potential impact force on the worker's body. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-146",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1054",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To ensure the worker will not strike a lower level in the event of a fall.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-147",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1055",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To calculate the distance traveled during a fall. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-148",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 69,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-39",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1056",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "39. What is swing fall, and why is it important to consider in fall protection calculations? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-149",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1057",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Swing fall is the distance a worker can swing after falling. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-150",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1058",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Swing fall occurs when a worker moves horizontally away from the anchor point, and it is  important to consider it to ensure the worker won't strike obstacles or the ground.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-151",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1059",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Swing fall is the distance a worker falls before the fall protection system engages. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-152",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 69,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-40",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1060",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "40. What is the primary purpose of warning lines in designated areas? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-153",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1061",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To prevent access to certain work areas. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-154",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1062",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To warn employees of an unprotected side or edge.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-155",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1063",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To guide the movement of mechanical equipment. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-156",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 69,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-41",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1064",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "41. What is a requirement for hole covers located in roadways and vehicular aisles? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-157",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1065",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Must be marked with the word "HOLE." ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-158",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1066",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Should support at least twice the maximum axle load of the largest vehicle expected to cross. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-159",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1067",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Should be capable of supporting the weight of employees only. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-160",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 69,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-42",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1068",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "42. What protective measures are mandated for employees working near wall openings? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-161",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1069",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Wearing reflective vests. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-162",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1070",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Guardrail system, safety net system, or personal fall arrest system. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-163",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1071",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Using handrails for support. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-164",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 69,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-43",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1072",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "43. Which of the following is true about handrails and stair rail systems? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-165",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1073",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. There must be a minimum clearance of 4 inches between handrails and any other object. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-166",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1074",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. The ends of handrails and stair rail systems should not present any projection hazards. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-167",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1075",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Opening in a stair rail system can exceed 24 inches at its least dimension. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-168",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 69,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-44",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1076",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "44. IAW 29 CFR 1926.105, when should safety nets be provided at workplaces? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-169",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1077",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. When workplaces are more than 25 feet above the ground or water surface. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-170",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1078",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. When workplaces are more than 10 feet above the ground. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-171",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1079",
                  "pageNumber": 69,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. When workplaces are more than 30 feet above the ground or water surface. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-172",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 69,
          "type": "list",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 69,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "list-45",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1080",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "45. IAW DAFMAN 91-203, what type of fall protection must occupants of buckets or platforms wear on  Mobile Elevated Work Platforms (MEWPs)? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-173",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1081",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Reflective vests. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-174",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1082",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Full-body harness and lanyard. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-175",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1083",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Hard hats. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-176",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 70,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-46",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1084",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "46. IAW 29 CFR 1926.451, employees on scaffolds over how many feet above ground level must be  protected from falls? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-177",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1085",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. 5 feet ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-178",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1086",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. 10 feet ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-179",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1087",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. 15 feet ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-180",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 70,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-47",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1088",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "47. What is a characteristic of ladder safety systems? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-181",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1089",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. They require continuous manual operation during climbing. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-182",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1090",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. They include cages or wells as integral components. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-183",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1091",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. They allow climbing with both hands free.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-184",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 70,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-48",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1092",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "48. IAW 29 CFR 1926.501, what fall protection systems can be used to protect workers from falling  when working on a leading edge? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-185",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1093",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Safety lighting systems. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-186",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1094",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Guardrail systems, safety net systems, or personal fall arrest systems.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-187",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1095",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Emergency evacuation procedures. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-188",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 70,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-49",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1096",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "49. True or False: For steel erecting, employees who are on a walking/working surface with an  unprotected edge more than 5 feet above a lower level must be protected by conventional fall  protection. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-189",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1097",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. True ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-190",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1098",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. False ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-191",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 70,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-50",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1099",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "50. For best practices for equipment storage, what are considerations for storing fall protection gear when  not in use? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-192",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1100",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Expose it to direct sunlight. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-193",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1101",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Store it in a moist environment. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-194",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1102",
                  "pageNumber": 70,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Hang it in a cool, dry place.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-195",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 70,
          "type": "list",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 70,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p-1103",
          "pageNumber": 71,
          "text": [
            {
              "text": "KNOWLEDGE CHECK – ANSWERS KEY ",
            },
          ],
          "type": "paragraph",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-51",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1104",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "1. What is the primary purpose of fall protection equipment? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-196",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1105",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To enhance worker productivity. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-197",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1106",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To mitigate the effect of falls. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-198",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1107",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To protect employees from serious injury or death that need to work in elevated locations  which meet the OSHA trigger heights. (pg. 9) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-199",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 71,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-52",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1108",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "2. IAW DAFMAN 91-203, what is the role of a Competent Person in the unit fall protection program? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-200",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1109",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Conducting fall hazard surveys. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-201",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1110",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Providing advice to the unit commander ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-202",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1111",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Administer and Manage the Unit Fall Protection Program. (pg. 9) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-203",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 71,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-53",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1112",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "3. IAW DAFMAN 91-203, who is ultimately responsible for the development and implementation of  the fall protection program that promotes a safe and healthful workplace? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-204",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1113",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Qualified Person ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-205",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1114",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Competent Person ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-206",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1115",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Unit Commander (pg. 10) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-207",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 71,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-54",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1116",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "4. True or False: Duties of the Installation Occupational Safety office include conducting thorough  annual review of fall protection program elements. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-208",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1117",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. True (pg. 10) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-209",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1118",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. False  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-210",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 71,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-55",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1119",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "5. Who assists in the fall hazard surveys and development of written fall protection and rescue  procedures? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-211",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1120",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Fire & Emergency Services (F&ES) Flight (pg. 10) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-212",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1121",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Unit Commander ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-213",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1122",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Authorized Rescuer ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-214",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 71,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-56",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1123",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "6. IAW DAFMAN 91-203, supervisor responsibilities include? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-215",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1124",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Responsible for the procurement of fall protection/fall arrest systems. (pg. 10) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-216",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1125",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Designation in writing by the Competent Person. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-217",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1126",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Delegates rescue team personnel. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-218",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 71,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-57",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1127",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "7. What is a common requirement for Trainers, Qualified, and Competent persons? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-219",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1128",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Designated in writing by the unit commander. (pg. 11) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-220",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1129",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Participate in the investigation of all incidents related to falls. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-221",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1130",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Implement a fall protection plan and rescue plan. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-222",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 71,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-58",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1131",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "8. When is fall protection retraining required? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-223",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1132",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. When changes in the workplace render previous training obsolete or inadequate. (pg. 12) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-224",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1133",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Only if there is an injury. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-225",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1134",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Once every three years. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-226",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 71,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-59",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1135",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "9. How often should recurring training be performed? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-227",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1136",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Quarterly ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-228",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1137",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Every 2 years ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-229",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1138",
                  "pageNumber": 71,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Annually (pg. 12) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-230",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 71,
          "type": "list",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 71,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "list-60",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1139",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "10. With what agency shall the Fall Protection Plan be coordinated? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-231",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1140",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Commander ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-232",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1141",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Occupational Safety Office (pg. 13) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-233",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1142",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. F&ES Flight ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-234",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 72,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-61",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1143",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "11. In what situations should falls from heights be reported? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-235",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1144",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Only if there is an injury. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-236",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1145",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Regardless of whether an injury or damage has occurred. (pg. 13) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-237",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1146",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Only if damage to property occurs. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-238",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 72,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-62",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1147",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "12. What is the purpose of a Fall Hazard Survey? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-239",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1148",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To determine the basic configuration of fall hazards. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-240",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1149",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To identify environmental factors affecting fall protection systems. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-241",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1150",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To help employers and safety professionals identify potential fall hazards and determine the  necessary steps to mitigate or eliminate them. (pg. 15) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-242",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 72,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-63",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1151",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "13. IAW DAFMAN 91-203 who typically leads the fall hazard survey team? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-243",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1152",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Competent or Qualified Person(s) (pg. 15) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-244",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1153",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Work Center Supervisors ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-245",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1154",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Installation Occupational Safety Office ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-246",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 72,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-64",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1155",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "14. True or False: A key aspects of a comprehensive Fall Hazard Survey is environmental factors  affecting the installation, use, inspection, maintenance, and dismantling of any fall protection system. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-247",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1156",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. True (pg. 16) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-248",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1157",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. False  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-249",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 72,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-65",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1158",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "15. The Fall Protection Program Assessment final report will be routed to the unit commander for review  and signature within how many days of completion? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-250",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1159",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. 5 ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-251",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1160",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. 10 (pg. 17) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-252",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1161",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. 30 ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-253",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 72,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-66",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1162",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "16. IAW DAFI 91-202 how often will the installation or tenant unit’s Occupational Safety Office  complete an assessment of Fall Protection Program requirements for each unit? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-254",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1163",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Annually (pg. 17) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-255",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1164",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Quarterly ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-256",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1165",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Every 2 years ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-257",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 72,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-67",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1166",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "17. IAW DAFMAN 91-203 a Rescue Plan will include all the following EXCEPT? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-258",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1167",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Procedures to contact the rescue agency if a fall occurs. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-259",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1168",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Actions to be taken by the organization to rescue fallen authorized personnel, when possible. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-260",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1169",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Steps to take when work is completed, e.g., clean up, storage. (pg. 18-19) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-261",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 72,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-68",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1170",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "18. What are the SIGNS of suspension trauma? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-262",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1171",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Increased heart rate and high blood pressure. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-263",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1172",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Severe headache and muscle pain. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-264",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1173",
                  "pageNumber": 72,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Faintness, nausea, breathlessness, and dizziness. (pg. 19) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-265",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 72,
          "type": "list",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 72,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "list-69",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1174",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "19. What are some examples of a fallen worker secondary hazards? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-266",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1175",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Broken bones, entanglement, shock. (pg. 20) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-267",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1176",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Heartburn, nausea, indigestion. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-268",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1177",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Sore throat, runny nose, cough.  ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-269",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 73,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-70",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1178",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "20. What is the primary approach outlined in the Hierarchy of Fall Protection for addressing fall hazards? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-270",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1179",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Fall Arrest Systems ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-271",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1180",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Administrative Controls ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-272",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1181",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Hazard Elimination (pg. 21) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-273",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 73,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-71",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1182",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "21. According to the Hierarchy of Fall Protection, which control method involves creating physical  barriers to prevent falls? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-274",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1183",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Fall Restraint Systems ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-275",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1184",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Passive Fall Protection (pg. 21) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-276",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1185",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Administrative Controls ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-277",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 73,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-72",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1186",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "22. Which type of fall protection involves devices like guardrails and nets that prevent falls but are not  directly connected to the employee? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-278",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1187",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Suspension System. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-279",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1188",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Passive Fall Protection. (pg. 23) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-280",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1189",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Positioning System. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-281",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 73,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-73",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1190",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "23. What is the purpose of a Retrieval System in fall protection? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-282",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1191",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To restrict an employee's range of movement. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-283",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1192",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To provide prompt rescue of employees in the event of a fall. (pg. 23) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-284",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1193",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To allow employees to lift and lower themselves along a vertical surface. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-285",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 73,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-74",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1194",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "24. True or False: There are NO exceptions to fall protection? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-286",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1195",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. True ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-287",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1196",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. False (pg. 24) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-288",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 73,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-75",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1197",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "25. Which of the following materials is NOT suitable for connectors in personal fall protection systems? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-289",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1198",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Stainless Steel ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-290",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1199",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Natural fiber (pg. 25) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-291",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1200",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Steel ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-292",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 73,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-76",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1201",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "26. What system consists of a body harness, anchorage, and connector? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-293",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1202",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. PFAS (pg. 26) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-294",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1203",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Positioning Systems ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-295",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1204",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Rope Descent System ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-296",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 73,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-77",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1205",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "27. IAW 29 CFR 1910.21 which of the following is NOT part of a Rope Descent System? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-297",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1206",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Descent device ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-298",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1207",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Horizontal lifeline (pg. 30) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-299",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1208",
                  "pageNumber": 73,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Chair (seatboard). ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-300",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 73,
          "type": "list",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 73,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "list-78",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1209",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "28. What is the purpose of a travel restraint system? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-301",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1210",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To arrest an employee in a fall. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-302",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1211",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To eliminate the possibility of an employee going over the edge of a walking-working  surface. (pg. 30) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-303",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1212",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To provide support on an elevated vertical surface. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-304",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 74,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-79",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1213",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "29. Which lifeline system is primarily used for tasks that require workers to move horizontally over a  large area without constantly disconnecting and reattaching to different anchor points? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-305",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1214",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Portable Gantry ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-306",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1215",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Horizontal Lifeline (pg. 31-32) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-307",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1216",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Rigid Rail System ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-308",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 74,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-80",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1217",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "30. Which lifeline system is typically used in environments like warehouses and factories, providing fall  arrest solutions with short arrest distances? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-309",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1218",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Horizontal Lifeline ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-310",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1219",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Rigid Rail System (pg. 32) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-311",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1220",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Portable Gantry ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-312",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 74,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-81",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1221",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "31. IAW 29 CFR 1910.21, what defines a low-slope roof? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-313",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1222",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Any roof with a slope greater than 4-foot in 12-foot. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-314",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1223",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Any roof that is flat or less than or equal to a ratio of 4-foot in 12-foot. (pg. 34) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-315",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1224",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Any roof with a slope greater than 6-foot in 12-foot. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-316",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 74,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-82",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1225",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "32. In webbing material, which material is more durable and rigid than nylon, and resists water  absorption? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-317",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1226",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Polyester (pg. 35) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-318",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1227",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Nylon ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-319",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1228",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Chemical resistant ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-320",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 74,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-83",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1229",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "33. When inspecting a lanyard prior to use, where should the inspection begin? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-321",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1230",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. In the middle of the lanyard. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-322",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1231",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. At one end of the lanyard working towards the other end. (pg. 38) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-323",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1232",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. From the hardware towards the rope or strap. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-324",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 74,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-84",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1233",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "34. What is the primary purpose of the impact indicator on a self-retracting device? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-325",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1234",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To determine the device's maximum allowable weight. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-326",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1235",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To signal whether the device has been exposed to fall forces and should be retired. (pg. 41) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-327",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1236",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To identify the manufacturer of the device. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-328",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 74,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-85",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1237",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "35. IAW 29 CFR 1910.140, anchorages used to attach personal fall protection equipment must be capable  of supporting at least how many pounds for each attached employee? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-329",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1238",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. 5,000 pounds. (pg. 42) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-330",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1239",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. 7,500 pounds. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-331",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1240",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. 10,000 pounds. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-332",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 74,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-86",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1241",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "36. IAW 29 CFR 1910.140, connectors must have a finish that is? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-333",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1242",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Painted. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-334",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1243",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Galvanized. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-335",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1244",
                  "pageNumber": 74,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Corrosion-resistant. (pg. 43) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-336",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 74,
          "type": "list",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 74,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "list-87",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1245",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "37. True or False: Maximum Arresting Force (MAF) refers to the highest force exerted on the body when  stopping a fall? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-337",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1246",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. True (pg. 45) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-338",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1247",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. False ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-339",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 75,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-88",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1248",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "38. What is the primary purpose of calculating fall clearance in a fall protection system? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-340",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1249",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To assess the potential impact force on the worker's body. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-341",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1250",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To ensure the worker will not strike a lower level in the event of a fall. (pg. 45) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-342",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1251",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To calculate the distance traveled during a fall. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-343",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 75,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-89",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1252",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "39. What is swing fall, and why is it important to consider in fall protection calculations? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-344",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1253",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Swing fall is the distance a worker can swing after falling. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-345",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1254",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Swing fall occurs when a worker moves horizontally away from the anchor point, and it is  important to consider it to ensure the worker won't strike obstacles or the ground. (pg. 46) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-346",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1255",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Swing fall is the distance a worker falls before the fall protection system engages. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-347",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 75,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-90",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1256",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "40. What is the primary purpose of warning lines in designated areas? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-348",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1257",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. To prevent access to certain work areas. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-349",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1258",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. To warn employees of an unprotected side or edge. (pg. 48) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-350",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1259",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. To guide the movement of mechanical equipment. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-351",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 75,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-91",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1260",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "41. What is a requirement for hole covers located in roadways and vehicular aisles? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-352",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1261",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Must be marked with the word "HOLE." ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-353",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1262",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Should support at least twice the maximum axle load of the largest vehicle expected to  cross. (pg. 50) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-354",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1263",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Should be capable of supporting the weight of employees only. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-355",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 75,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-92",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1264",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "42. What protective measures are mandated for employees working near wall openings? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-356",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1265",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Wearing reflective vests. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-357",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1266",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Guardrail system, safety net system, or personal fall arrest system. (pg. 51) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-358",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1267",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Using handrails for support. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-359",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 75,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-93",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1268",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "43. Which of the following is true about handrails and stair rail systems? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-360",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1269",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. There must be a minimum clearance of 4 inches between handrails and any other object. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-361",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1270",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. The ends of handrails and stair rail systems should not present any projection hazards. (pg.  52) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-362",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1271",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Opening in a stair rail system can exceed 24 inches at its least dimension. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-363",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 75,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-94",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1272",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "44. IAW 29 CFR 1926.105, when should safety nets be provided at workplaces? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-364",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1273",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. When workplaces are more than 25 feet above the ground or water surface. (pg. 53) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-365",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1274",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. When workplaces are more than 10 feet above the ground. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-366",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1275",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. When workplaces are more than 30 feet above the ground or water surface. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-367",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 75,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-95",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1276",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "45. IAW DAFMAN 91-203, what type of fall protection must occupants of buckets or platforms wear on  Mobile Elevated Work Platforms (MEWPs)? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-368",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1277",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Reflective vests. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-369",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1278",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Full-body harness and lanyard. (pg. 55) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-370",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1279",
                  "pageNumber": 75,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Hard hats. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-371",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 75,
          "type": "list",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 75,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
    {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "list-96",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1280",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "46. IAW 29 CFR 1926.451, employees on scaffolds over how many feet above ground level must be  protected from falls? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-372",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1281",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. 5 feet ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-373",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1282",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. 10 feet (pg. 56) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-374",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1283",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. 15 feet ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-375",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 76,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-97",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1284",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "47. What is a characteristic of ladder safety systems? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-376",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1285",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. They require continuous manual operation during climbing. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-377",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1286",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. They include cages or wells as integral components. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-378",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1287",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. They allow climbing with both hands free. (pg. 58) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-379",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 76,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-98",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1288",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "48. IAW 29 CFR 1926.501, what fall protection systems can be used to protect workers from falling  when working on a leading edge? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-380",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1289",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Safety lighting systems. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-381",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1290",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Guardrail systems, safety net systems, or personal fall arrest systems. (pg. 59) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-382",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1291",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Emergency evacuation procedures. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-383",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 76,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-99",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1292",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "49. True or False: For steel erecting, employees who are on a walking/working surface with an  unprotected edge more than 5 feet above a lower level must be protected by conventional fall  protection. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-384",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1293",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. True ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-385",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1294",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. False (pg. 60) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-386",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 76,
          "type": "list",
        },
        {
          "id": "list-100",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1295",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "50. For best practices for equipment storage, what are considerations for storing fall protection gear when  not in use? ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-387",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1296",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "A. Expose it to direct sunlight. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-388",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1297",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "B. Store it in a moist environment. ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-389",
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "id": "p-1298",
                  "pageNumber": 76,
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "text": "C. Hang it in a cool, dry place. (pg. 61) ",
                    },
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph",
                },
              ],
              "id": "li-390",
            },
          ],
          "ordered": false,
          "pageNumber": 76,
          "type": "list",
        },
      ],
      "height": 792,
      "pageNumber": 76,
      "warnings": [],
      "width": 612,
    },
  ],
